  "id": "Compound::DB08800 - Gene::3269",
  "verbalization": "Chloropyramine is closely related to Mepyramine and Pheniramine, which both bind to Hrh1, suggesting a potential mechanism of action through shared molecular interactions. The evidence indicates that Chloropyramine, through its resemblance to Mepyramine and Pheniramine, may share a similar binding profile with Hrh1, thereby contributing to its interaction with the target. The lowest common ancestors of these compounds point to the Histamine-1 Receptor Antagonist class and Organic Compounds, highlighting a possible pathway where Chloropyramine's structural similarities to other antihistamines could influence its interaction with Hrh1. The integration of these pathways suggests that Chloropyramine may act as a competitive inhibitor of Hrh1, leveraging its structural resemblance to other antihistamines to modulate the receptor's activity.",
